course: dictionary
lesson: 10314
title: Toxic: poison and harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toxic is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a toxic plant, a toxic gas. It means poisonous, able to harm or kill living things if they swallow it, breathe it in or touch it. «Toxic fumes» and «toxic waste» are about dangerous substances.
explain: Toxic can also describe behaviour. When it describes a friendship or a relationship, it means harmful and unkind. «A toxic friendship» is one that keeps making you feel bad, even though it does not poison your body.
explain: The two meanings share one idea: something that does harm. Look at the words around toxic to tell which meaning is used. Poison, fumes and waste point to the first meaning; nasty, unkind or making you feel bad point to the second.
fact: Toxic means poisonous, able to harm or kill living things.
fact: «Toxic» can describe a substance, as in «toxic fumes», «toxic waste» or «toxic to dogs».
fact: «Toxic» can describe behaviour, as in «a toxic friendship», which is harmful and unkind.
fact: Some plants, berries, mushrooms and cleaning products can be toxic, so never taste anything you do not know.
fact: Warning symbols on bottles show if a product is toxic, so read them before you touch.
exercise: «Warning symbols on bottles show if a product is corrosive, toxic, flammable or harmful.» What does toxic mean here? | Very heavy | Bright and shiny | *Poisonous, able to harm or kill if swallowed or breathed in | Easy to open
exercise: Which of these could be toxic, so you must never taste it? | A cup of water | A slice of bread | An apple from the shop | *A wild berry you do not know
exercise: Mia says, «He is toxic, he makes me feel bad every day.» What does toxic mean here? | *Harmful and unkind | Poisonous to fish | Playful and funny | Very hot
test: What does «a toxic friendship» describe? | *A friendship that is harmful and unkind | A friendship that happens at school | A friendship with two best friends | A friendship that is very old
test: Which word on a bottle warns that it could harm you if swallowed? | Round | Empty | Bright | *Toxic
exam: Which sentence uses toxic in the sense of harmful and unkind? | «The inland taipan has the most toxic venom of any land snake.» | *«Players who are nasty on purpose are called toxic.» | «Mining can poison rivers with toxic metals.» | «Warning symbols on bottles show if a product is toxic.»
